WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.045 --> 00:00:08.999
As Scrooge followed the strange ghost, the darkness of its cloak seemed to expand and swallow him up.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.635
He blinked and saw they were on a bustling city street.

3
00:00:13.636 --> 00:00:19.331
It was daytime, and several businessmen were gathered here and there, talking.

4
00:00:19.332 --> 00:00:22.587
The spirit stopped beside three men.

5
00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:26.665
"Did you hear?" a stout man was saying.

6
00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:30.908
"The devil has welcomed back one of its own."

7
00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:37.955
"Yes, I heard. I don't know how it happened, though," a very tall man said.

8
00:00:37.956 --> 00:00:43.170
"I only know he's dead. When did he die?"

9
00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:48.972
"Last night, I believe." The third man checked his gold watch.

10
00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:55.765
"What was the matter with him anyway? I thought he'd never die."

11
00:00:55.766 --> 00:01:00.262
"Who knows." The tall man yawned.

12
00:01:00.263 --> 00:01:05.107
"More importantly, what has he done with his money?"

13
00:01:05.108 --> 00:01:09.141
The man with the gold watch chuckled.

14
00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:13.659
"He didn't leave it to any of us, that's for sure!"

15
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:19.029
"Well, it's going to be a very cheap and small funeral," the tall man said.

16
00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.995
"Should we go, just so at least a few people show up?"

17
00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:32.917
The stout man looked interested. "I'd go if a nice lunch is provided."

18
00:01:32.918 --> 00:01:37.280
"I know these men," Scrooge said to the ghost.

19
00:01:37.281 --> 00:01:40.320
"They're well known around the city.

20
00:01:40.321 --> 00:01:46.016
But why do you want me to hear them? Who are they discussing?

21
00:01:46.017 --> 00:01:50.718
It can't be Jacob Marley, because his death happened in the past.

22
00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:54.440
You're supposed to be showing me the future."

23
00:01:54.441 --> 00:01:57.660
Suddenly the street disappeared.

24
00:01:57.661 --> 00:02:04.156
Scrooge was now walking through an unfamiliar part of the city with small, shabby houses.

25
00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:09.762
The streets were narrow and dirty, and the people looked tired and thin.

26
00:02:09.763 --> 00:02:14.391
Rats darted here and there, bold and bright eyed.

27
00:02:14.392 --> 00:02:22.000
Even the snow seemed different, with soot and dust settling upon it as soon as it touched the ground.

28
00:02:22.001 --> 00:02:30.013
The spirit led Scrooge to a grubby shop where iron, rags, bottles, and other items were bought and sold.

29
00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:36.130
A gray-haired shopkeeper sat among the goods, smoking a pipe.

30
00:02:36.131 --> 00:02:40.951
A woman entered the shop carrying a large bundle.

31
00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:45.652
Moments later a second woman came in with a bundle of her own.

32
00:02:45.653 --> 00:02:50.488
They were soon followed by a man in a faded black coat.

33
00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:57.023
When all three seemed startled to see the others, the shopkeeper laughed.

34
00:02:57.024 --> 00:03:01.495
"You look surprised to see one another," he said.

35
00:03:01.496 --> 00:03:08.597
"But I heard your employer died, and so I'm not surprised to see any of you.

36
00:03:08.598 --> 00:03:13.123
I'll let the housekeeper show me what she has brought first.

37
00:03:13.124 --> 00:03:20.939
The laundrywoman can go second. The undertaker's assistant will be third."

38
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.866
The housekeeper dropped her bundle on the shop floor.

39
00:03:24.867 --> 00:03:28.229
Her expression was guilty and defiant.

40
00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.725
"Every person has a right to take care of themselves.

41
00:03:31.726 --> 00:03:35.980
Though I never met him, I know he always did."

42
00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:39.861
"That's true, indeed!" the laundrywoman said.

43
00:03:39.862 --> 00:03:43.317
"He was always thinking about himself!"

44
00:03:43.318 --> 00:03:46.253
The housekeeper kicked open her bundle.

45
00:03:46.254 --> 00:03:50.805
Inside were a couple of blankets and a set of bed curtains.

46
00:03:50.806 --> 00:03:55.512
"A dead man will not miss these things."

47
00:03:55.513 --> 00:04:01.383
"He won't miss these either," the laundrywoman said, opening her own bundle.

48
00:04:01.384 --> 00:04:07.275
It contained men's clothing, a few silver teaspoons, and a worn pair of boots.

49
00:04:07.276 --> 00:04:12.488
"His things didn't help him in the end," the undertaker's assistant said.

50
00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:19.001
"They could not have comforted him while he lay gasping out his last breath, all by himself."

51
00:04:19.002 --> 00:04:21.180
The man opened the bundle.

52
00:04:21.181 --> 00:04:27.059
It held only a pencil case, some buttons, and a few other small things.

53
00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:32.876
Scrooge watched in horror as the shopkeeper examined everything before him.

54
00:04:32.877 --> 00:04:37.999
"These servants stole from their employer!" Scrooge cried.

55
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.413
"They have no respect for him, even when he's dead!"

56
00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:46.118
As usual, the spirit didn't answer.

57
00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:49.319
Scrooge sighed in frustration.

58
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.628
Then he suddenly realized why the ghost was showing him these scenes.

59
00:04:54.629 --> 00:05:05.662
"Oh!" he said. "You're telling me, spirit, that the situation of this unfortunate man could be my situation too.

60
00:05:05.663 --> 00:05:13.239
You want me to know that I must change or I will share his fate. Is that correct?"

61
00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:18.276
The spirit lifted its finger, and the grubby shop disappeared.

62
00:05:18.277 --> 00:05:22.134
Now the two of them were standing in Scrooge's bedroom.

63
00:05:22.135 --> 00:05:27.753
A familiar form lay on the bed, not moving or even breathing.

64
00:05:27.754 --> 00:05:35.156
"Oh!" Scrooge gazed in horror at the lifeless body on the bed.

65
00:05:35.157 --> 00:05:40.559
"The dead man whom everyone is discussing—it's me!"

66
00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.517
The spirit nodded slowly.

67
00:05:43.518 --> 00:05:48.508
"I promise, I have learned my lesson!" Scrooge said.

68
00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:54.383
"But surely there must be at least one person who will feel strong emotions about my death.

69
00:05:54.384 --> 00:06:03.922
If so, please show that person to me."

